<title>JAPAN: FORECAST-Breakdown of June tankan forecasts.</title>
<headline>FORECAST-Breakdown of June tankan forecasts.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-06-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Below is a breakdown of forecasts by private think-tanks for major manufacturers' and non-manufacturers' diffusion indices in the Bank of Japan's (BOJ) June quarterly corporate survey, known as the tankan.</p>
<p>The think-tanks were polled by Reuters this week.</p>
<p>The BOJ survey will released at 8.50 a.m. on June 25 (2350 GMT June 24). The previous survey was conducted in March and released on April 2.</p>
<p>			Major mfrs   Major non-mfrs</p>
<p>March actual	  +2		 -6</p>
<p>March forecast</p>
<p>  for June	    -1		 -7</p>
<p>*************************************************</p>
<p>Lehman Brothers     -2		 -7</p>
<p>HSCB James Capel     0		 -8</p>
<p>BZW		     +1		 -3</p>
<p>Merrill Lynch	 +3		 -3</p>
<p>Salomon Bros	  -3		-10</p>
<p>Schroders	     +3		 -7</p>
<p>ING Barings	   +2		 -5</p>
<p>JP Morgan	     +4		 -6</p>
<p>CS First Boston     -2		 -5</p>
<p>BOT-Mitsubishi</p>
<p>    Securities	+4		 -4</p>
<p>IBJ		     +1		 -7</p>
<p>DKB Research	  +3		 -5</p>
<p>Fuji Research	 -3		 -9</p>
<p>Sanwa Research	-4		 -8</p>
<p>Nihon Research	-2		 -7</p>
<p>Sakura Securities   +2		 -4</p>
